WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:07.481
Shifts shows who’s on duty, plans the week, and shows how it went. In this video, you’ll plan a shift and start your own.

2
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:16.737
Open Operations, and choose Shifts. My shifts shows whether you’re on duty, your shifts coming up, and your hours planned and worked this week.

3
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.043
Past shifts lists what you worked, with clock-in and out times, breaks, and any lateness.

4
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:31.375
Team schedule shows the whole week, with a row for each person. Each shift is coloured by how it went: worked, on duty, upcoming, late, or missed.

5
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:39.193
Managers plan the week. Click Add shift, and pick the person, the location, the day and the times. Add a role if you like.

6
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:48.849
Save, and Lena’s Saturday shift is on the schedule. One person can’t have two shifts at once, and with Training on, an expired card stops the shift.

7
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.887
Copy last week copies every shift into this week, and skips any that would clash.

8
00:00:54.333 --> 00:01:02.269
To start your own shift, tap Start my shift on the On duty strip, and pick where you are. Take a break and End my shift work the same way.

9
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:09.539
Or just tell Assist, start my shift. And if you use Square, starting and ending a shift clocks you in and out there too.

10
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:17.931
That’s shifts. Next in the Features series: Order Tracking. You’ll find every guide at worklynq.com/docs.

